{
  "id": "proj-floating-nightstand",
  "slug": "floating-nightstand",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Floating Nightstand",
  "summary": "A wall-hung drawer box on a hidden cleat. Clears the floor and fits a phone charger inside.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 5,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "From the 3/4 in plywood cut a 16 x 12 in top and bottom, two 5 1/2 x 11 1/4 in sides and a 14 1/4 x 5 3/8 in drawer front. Rip a 3 in strip at 45 degrees with the saw guide and cut it into two 14 1/2 in cleats.",
    "Iron edge banding onto every front edge and the ends of the top and bottom, then trim it flush. It is far easier before assembly.",
    "Drill pocket holes on the inside faces of the sides and glue and screw them between the top and bottom, flush at the front and set 3/4 in in from the back. The back stays open.",
    "Glue and screw one cleat under the top at the back, bevel facing down and toward the box. This is the half that hooks over the wall cleat, hidden inside the case.",
    "Build the drawer from 1/2 in plywood: two 4 1/2 x 10 in sides and two 4 1/2 x 12 1/2 in ends, glued and screwed through the sides, with the 1/4 in bottom glued and screwed underneath. Bore a 2 in hole in the back and press in the grommet for the charger cable.",
    "Mount the 10 in slides in the case and on the drawer, slide it in, and screw the false front on from inside with a 1/16 in gap all round. Fit the pull.",
    "Sand to 220 and wipe on three coats of poly. Screw the wall cleat level, bevel up and toward the wall, into a stud with 3 in screws and into toggle anchors where there is no stud, then lift the case onto it. Route your own charger cable from the outlet through the grommet with a slack loop so the drawer can open."
  ],
